  "details": "   * Non-maintainer upload by the TuxCare ELS team.\n   * CVE-2026-119371: limit the nesting depth of common table expressions\n     with SQLITE_LIMIT_EXPR_DEPTH to prevent a stack overflow on deeply\n     chained CTEs.\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-119371.patch\n   * CVE-2026-119373: fix a heap buffer overflow in fts5MergeRowidLists()\n     when merging detail=none prefix doclists that contain negative rowids.\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-119373.patch\n   * CVE-2026-119375: fully initialize the page buffer when a WAL frame is\n     smaller than the database page, so stale page-cache memory is not\n     disclosed.\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-119375.patch",
